-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510176} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6e028ab-a36c-5469-ba63-ab22fef00ac7" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d451e41-c662-5263-b3f7-8483ecaa8976" :question/math-academy-id "q-342964" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-2{x}^{2}+4$ defined on $[-3,3).$  Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $6$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-4x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+4∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-4x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=3$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-3,3),$\n\n- continuous on $[-3,3),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-3)=F(3),$ if we extend the value at $x=3$ using the formula $F(x)=-2{x}^{2}+4.$\n\nTherefore, the $6$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2{x}^{2}+4) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-2)+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -4x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{72(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})) \\\\ -4x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-24(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3}) \\\\ -4x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{24(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317373 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0933967e-8a36-5c98-9978-af481d6e1c97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315163} {:answer/id #uuid "6668d210-3666-5a78-bdab-b36c77b23f20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315688} {:answer/id #uuid "c224d4a5-a69e-51bd-b87f-2a11fff0f518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c224d4a5-a69e-51bd-b87f-2a11fff0f518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "continuous" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316209} :answer-field/id #uuid "206ee1d4-18b6-5317-b71a-60ab4bb59aa9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316623} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "308e0394-5c17-5c18-8ff0-e80da631f21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db