}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d516aab-95d3-5da5-b47b-419bd5928c22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315647} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5483c1d-8db2-580c-a05c-15ddc746e3b3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186317127}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "295865d5-976f-59ac-b940-a1bbaaa4904a" :question/math-academy-id "q-343247" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $10$-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5$ defined on $[-5,5).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of the Fourier series of the $10$-periodic extension of $G(x)=-\\frac{3}{2}x$ from the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5∼-\\frac{5}{4}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}}\nand\n{{field-3}}\non $R,$ we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{2}x∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-4}}\\cdot {{field-5}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=5$ and we are already given the coefficients ${a}_{0}$ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼-\\frac{5}{4}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that \n\n- the function $F$ is continuously differentiable on $(-5,5),$\n\n- continuous on $[-5,5),$ and\n\n- satisfies $F(-5)=F(5),$ if we extend the value at $x=5$ using the formula $F(x)=-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5.$\n\nTherefore, the $10$-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{continuous}$ and $\\text{piecewise smooth}$ on $R,$ so we may differentiate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{3}{4}{x}^{2}+5) & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\frac{5}{4})+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼0+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{75(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}}\\cdot (-\\frac{n\\pi }{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{-15(-1)^{n+1}}{n\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5}) \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}x & ∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{15(-1)^{n}}{n\\pi }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{5})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317374 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186221450 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2e37d37-007c-569b-a44c-cb6a9d075371" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Fourier Series"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cae41e16-6610-5e58-9108-5de3295f0ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316263} {:answer/id #uuid "fa388873-f615-5353-85a4-676842681e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa388873-f615-5353-85a4-676842681e6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316516} :answer-field/id #uuid "4af30516-d825-5430-b585-c2b9688b4